2026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":6.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"outlook","statement":"NTPC plans to expand its total capacity portfolio to 150 gigawatts by FY32 and to 250 gigawatts by FY37.","quote":"Guided by our new corporate plan, NTPC is charting an ambitious growth trajectory, targeting a capacity portfolio of 150 gigawatts by FY32 and on to 250 gigawatts by FY37.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":9.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"guidance","statement":"NTPC aims to add 7 to 8 gigawatts of renewable energy capacity in FY27, contingent on transmission infrastructure.","quote":"During FY26, we have added around 4.2 gigawatt, and further, subject to transmission infrastructure, we are targeting to add another 7 gigawatts to 8 gigawatts for the renewable capacity in FY27.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":10.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"guidance","statement":"Management expects to maintain a dividend payout ratio between 36% and 40%.","quote":"It will be hovering around 36% to 40%. That has been the payout ratio, and we would be comfortable with that.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":21.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"demand","statement":"India's annual electricity requirement is projected to rise from 1,708 billion units in FY26 to 8,100 billion units by FY50.","quote":"India's electricity requirement is projected to grow from 1,708 billion units in FY26 to 8,100 billion units by FY50 and further to 13,000 billion units by FY70.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":8.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capex","statement":"NTPC estimates a capital expenditure of INR 5,97,000 crores between FY28 and FY32 primarily for renewable energy projects.","quote":"The second phasing, comprising five years from FY28 to FY32, total capex would be INR5,97,000 crores, driven primarily by renewable energy projects as we move towards our goal of becoming a 60 gigawatt company in the renewable space.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":10.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capacity","statement":"NTPC and Mahagenco acquired the 1,350 MW Sinnar thermal power station and aim to commission a unit this calendar year.","quote":"We have acquired, along with Mahagenco, Sinnar thermal power station, which is 1,350 megawatt, and we are putting best efforts to commission one unit in this calendar year and then one after the other.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":5.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"debt","statement":"NTPC's weighted average interest rate on borrowings dropped to 5.98% compared to 6.61% in FY25.","quote":"The weighted average interest rate on the borrowing stood at 5.98% compared to 6.61% in the financial year 25.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"debt","statement":"The company's debt-equity ratio improved to 1.32 while maintaining healthy cash accruals.","quote":"The debt-equity ratio has improved to 1.32, while stable cash accruals provide ample headroom to support future capital expenditure and resource mobilization.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":12.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"initiatives","statement":"NTPC is establishing a green hydrogen hub at Pudimadakka to help make India a global green hydrogen leader.","quote":"NTPC is developing a flagship green hydrogen hub at Pudimadakka, as we have shared with you already, to support India's emergence as a global leader in green hydrogen.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":11.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"industry","statement":"India reached 50% cumulative installed power capacity from non-fossil fuel sources in June 2025.","quote":"India further achieved the milestone of 50% cumulative installed capacity from non-fossil fuel source in June 2025, five years ahead of its target set by its Nationally Determined Contribution to Paris Agreement commitment.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":8.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"tone","statement":"positive","quote":"With this, I would like to assure all of you that we will continue to put tireless efforts to maximize profitability in a sustainable manner and create value for the shareholders year after year.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_02082026151004_6__Disclosure_for_Transcript_of_Investor_Presentation_Final.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"industry","statement":"India's total installed power capacity grew by 13% year-over-year to reach 549 GW by June 2026, driven by renewable energy.","quote":"Installed Capacity Rising at Record Pace, Led by Renewables 549GW Total installed capacity, June 2026 + 13% YoY (from 485 GW)","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_27072026160924_4_Disclosure_for_Investor_Presentation_signed.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"industry","statement":"Non-fossil fuel sources, including 237 GW of renewable energy, reached 297 GW, representing a 22% year-over-year increase.","quote":"297 GW (incl 237 GW RE) Non-Fossil Fuel Source +22% Yo Y (from 243 GW)","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_27072026160924_4_Disclosure_for_Investor_Presentation_signed.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"initiatives","statement":"The Pudimadaka hydrogen hub is planned to produce green chemicals, including green ammonia, green methanol, sustainable aviation fuel, and green urea.","quote":"Green Chemical Production : Green Ammonia: 4300 TPD Green Methanol: 1 500 TPD Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) : 600 TPD Green Urea: 1000 TPD","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_27072026160924_4_Disclosure_for_Investor_Presentation_signed.pdf","page":23.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capacity","statement":"NTPC is developing a 2.8 GW pressurized heavy water reactor nuclear project at Mahi Banswara in Rajasthan.","quote":"Developing PHWR based 2.8 GW (4 x 700MW) Project at Mahi Banswara, Rajasthan","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_27072026160924_4_Disclosure_for_Investor_Presentation_signed.pdf","page":21.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capacity","statement":"NTPC has an operational capacity exceeding 90 GW, representing approximately 24% of electricity generation and 17% of capacity in India.","quote":"Operational capacity of over 90 GW - 24% share in electricity with - 17% share in capacity","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/9425178051_27072026160924_4_Disclosure_for_Investor_Presentation_signed.pdf","pag